- 18. Glossary}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- 19. GitHub update checks and Auto update}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- 20. Duplicate-folder cleanup utility - tlo-deleteDupes}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- 21. Research log lookup - tlo-research}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
1. What TLO Inventory does}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
TLO Inventory provides full inventory, incremental Add Shows processing, audio tagging, inventory searching, log research, and artist-database searching. The source bundle contains the TLO application sources, tests, documentation, and application distribution utilities. The independently versioned GitHub Build Process is distributed separately and is not included in the TLO source bundle. The separate distribution ZIP contains native end-user applications for Windows, macOS, and generic Linux. The generic Linux applications are also used when running under WSL; there is no separate WSL application directory or WSL build.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
The full inventory function scans configured music roots, identifies core show metadata, prepares searchable setlist text, and builds the inventory output used by the included search tools.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Full Inventory scans configured music roots and rebuilds the inventory outputs.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Add Shows adds new content to an existing inventory without rerunning the full scan.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Standalone Tag and inventory-time Tag in Place write audio metadata when you choose to tag files. Tag Copy and Tag Copy/Delete Original are Full Inventory modes, not standalone Tagger functions.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- The included Search app searches the completed bootlist and setlist files after the distribution is extracted into TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Research searches the comp and meta logs by artist plus date, venue, or date and is available from the Inventory GUI and the standalone tlo-research console app.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
2. Quick Start}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Use this path for a first non-destructive inventory. The detailed installation, volume-name, and option sections follow later in the manual.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
1. Extract a complete platform ZIP directly into the folder that will be TLOHome. Do not run TLO from inside the ZIP.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
2. Confirm that TLOHome/TLO_DBs contains artists.sqlite and venues.txt.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
3. Set the TLOHome environment variable, or launch the GUI with --TLOHome followed by the full TLOHome path.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
4. Put one music root in TLOHome/toBeInventoried.txt, or enter one root in Search Path. A visible volume prefix such as [Archive]E:\\Music is strongly recommended.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
5. Start the Inventory GUI. For the first run, leave Tag in Place, Tag Copy, Tag Copy/Delete Original, Rename Compliantly, and Convert shn cleared.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
6. Select Dry run and click Inventory. Review the proposed show names and any planned tags without changing files.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
7. Clear Dry run and click Inventory again when the review is satisfactory. Confirm the settings in Review Operation and click Start.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
8. After completion, open TLOHome/bootlist.csv, TLOHome/setlists, the completion summary, and View Issues. Detailed logs are under TLOHome/logs.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\qc{
