\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
First-run safety: Dry run performs metadata and tag planning but does not write tags, convert SHN files, rename folders, copy or delete content, or replace inventory output.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
3. Installation package and TLOHome layout}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Each release has a source bundle and eight platform distribution ZIPs: complete and update packages for Windows onefile, Windows onedir, generic Linux, and macOS. Names follow TLO_V1.6Build448_complete_<platform>.zip and TLO_V1.6Build448_update_<platform>.zip. Use a complete package for a new installation. Use the matching update package only to refresh an existing TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The source bundle contains the current requirements DOCX, the current RTF user manual, TLO application source, tests, and application distribution utilities. It contains no GitHub Build Process artifacts; that independently versioned process is distributed separately. Complete distributions include the current RTF user manual, FAQ, required databases, starter files, release information, checksums, and malware-scan receipts. Update distributions contain only the matching application payload and update metadata so they do not overwrite user data.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
TLOHome/\line   apps/\line     Windows/\line       tlo-ggi.exe\line       tlo-gi.exe\line       tlo-research.exe\line       tlo-tag.exe\line       tlo-deleteDupes.cmd\line       tlo-gsi.exe\line       search-artist-db.exe\line       _internal/              Windows onedir package only\line     macOS/\line       tlo-ggi\line       tlo-gi\line       tlo-research\line       tlo-tag\line       tlo-deleteDupes\line       tlo-gsi\line       search-artist-db\line     Linux/\line       tlo-ggi\line       tlo-gi\line       tlo-research\line       tlo-tag\line       tlo-deleteDupes\line       tlo-gsi\line       search-artist-db\line   TLO_DBs/\line     artists.sqlite\line     venues.txt\line   debug/  dups/  logs/  readyForXfer/  setlists/  staged/\line   README_FIRST.txt\line   TLO-FAQ.txt\line   TLO_Inventory_User_Manual_v448.rtf\line   toBeInventoried.txt}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Every complete distribution includes tlo-gsi, tlo-research, search-artist-db, TLO_DBs/artists.sqlite, and TLO_DBs/venues.txt. The generic Linux applications are also used under WSL. The Windows onedir package places the six PyInstaller executables directly in apps/Windows with one shared apps/Windows/_internal folder, plus tlo-deleteDupes.cmd and its private runtime; keep that folder with the executables and replace the whole apps/Windows folder when switching between onefile and onedir layouts.}
