Shows Review Operation and then runs either the non-destructive Dry run or the full inventory using Search Path override if supplied, otherwise toBeInventoried.txt.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft82\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5253\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10424\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Pause}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Pauses full inventory between filesystem operations. Does not apply to Add Shows.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft82\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5253\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10424\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Resume}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Resumes a paused full inventory. Repeated Resume clicks report only when a pause is active.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Performance modes}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Search-path worker count is capped by the number of search paths queued for that run. Postprocess setlist/bootlist export uses a separate bounded worker pool after scanning finishes.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- gentle: best when using external drives, spinning disks, or Windows desktops where responsiveness matters. Uses 1 worker by default.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- balanced: moderate parallelism. GUI and CLI default performance mode. Typically uses up to 2 workers by default.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- fast: higher normal throughput, usually up to the CPU count by default.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- extreme: speed-first for inventory traversal. Search-path worker dispatch has no performance-mode worker cap unless Max Workers is set to a positive value. Postprocess still uses a bounded thread pool and honors Max Workers when set. Extreme does not skip non-compliant tag checks.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
10. Compliant versus non-compliant mode}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Compliant mode}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Use Compliant mode when folders intentionally follow predictable naming. The main supported forms, in precedence order, are String1 Date String2, String1 - String2 Date when a complete date occurs at a String2 boundary, String1 - String2, and String1 Date. For Date, TLO first looks for yyyy-mm-dd-style dates, including legitimate partial forms such as 19xx-xx-xx and 20xx-xx-xx, and then accepted year ranges before falling back to older date-recognition rules. Century-known 19xx/20xx partial years require the remaining month/day components to stay unknown. In compliant mode, FLAC tags are not read or used. Compliant cannot be combined with Rename Compliantly.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- String1 Date String2: String1 is the artist text, Date is normalized, and String2 is kept as the trailing show text unless online lookup fills venue/location. By default, a matched alias is written using the Artist DB master name. Check As-Is Artist Name to preserve String1 as written.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- String1 - String2 Date: after String1 Date String2 fails, TLO checks whether String2 begins or ends with one complete performance date. The date is normalized and assigned as Date, while the remaining String2 text stays raw as the album/show/venue tail. Example: The Georgia Satellites - Santa Cruz 01-17-87 becomes The Georgia Satellites 1987-01-17 Santa Cruz. Bare years, ranges, partial dates, and dates embedded in the middle of String2 do not trigger this refinement.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- String1 - String2: when the boundary-date refinement does not match, String2 is treated as an album/show tail and no Date is assigned. A parenthetical-only tail such as (Live) is preserved.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Every final Show Name retains all trailing parenthetical items in their original order. TLO captures them from the original folder name before cleaning the path for artist, date, venue, and location parsing, then restores them after normalization. A recognized performance qualifier such as Early Show or Late Show is also retained as a parenthesized suffix when it is not already present. This applies to Full Inventory, Add Shows, Dry run output, folder renames, bootlist rows, setlist names, and Album tags. For example, Danny Gatton 1994-03-13 Bottom Line NYC (set 2) becomes Danny Gatton 1994-03-13 Bottom Line New York, NY (set 2).}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- String1 Date: fallback when no String2 exists; show name becomes Artist Date. Artist output follows the As-Is Artist Name checkbox.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Standard video wrapper folders such as VIDEO_TS or BDMV can resolve from parent path components.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- The Billboard MP3 year-folder special case applies only when all inventoried music files are .mp3, the folder name is a four-digit year from 1959 through 2005, and billboard appears somewhere in the path. The exported setlist filename for this special case uses the same four-digit year.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Non-compliant mode}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Use Non-compliant mode when folder names vary or contain partial or uncertain metadata. Non-compliant mode uses more evidence and tries to fill missing metadata without overwriting earlier trusted fields. As-Is Artist Name applies here too: unchecked uses an Artist DB master name for an unambiguous alias match; checked preserves the artist text from the metadata source that identified the show.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Reads FLAC ALBUMARTIST, ARTIST, ALBUM, and DATE tags before weaker path artist fallback. Within low-priority FLAC artist evidence, ALBUMARTIST is considered before ARTIST. Before Artist DB lookup, an explicitly dash-delimited or parenthesized terminal performance qualifier such as Early Show or Late Show is separated from a tag artist candidate. If the normal exact lookup then misses, TLO may ignore apostrophe characters for one retry, but accepts the result only when it identifies one unique Artist DB master. Tag values containing unknown or track are treated as blank for artist purposes, and tag evidence does not override stronger $slam, structured setlist, selected-setlist-filename, explicit folder-pattern/commercial-release, or other established higher-confidence artist evidence.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Searches folder and path text for artist, date, venue, and location clues, including known artist names and aliases. Generic path scanning does not promote an Artist DB term found entirely inside the parsed venue/location tail of a date-bearing folder; Attic inside Eddie's Attic is therefore venue text, while an exact artist directory named Attic remains eligible. Short no-space-date artist abbreviations such as gd in gd1977-05-08 are deliberately weak evidence: TLO first checks stronger tags, full DB-backed path names, selected-setlist metadata/filename evidence, and other structured sources. Only if those fail may the abbreviation resolve through artists.sqlite as a final local fallback; an enabled artist/date online lookup may corroborate it but does not promote abbreviation evidence above stronger sources.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Recognizes the non-compliant Date Artist Venue Location path pattern when a date begins the folder component. The Artist must be the longest unique Artist DB match beginning immediately after the date. A venue must remain after removing the Artist, and the remainder must also parse into City plus Region or Country. For example, 1997-04-05 Genesis Old Pub London England becomes Genesis 1997-04-05 Old Pub London, England. TLO rejects 1990-07-10 Palace Melbourne Australia under this pattern because removing Palace leaves only a location and no venue.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- For an ordinary non-compliant String1 - String2 name, TLO checks String2 for a complete performance date before using the generic Artist - Album fallback. It also accepts a supported partial date when that date is at the beginning or end of String2; a partial date embedded in the middle of album-like text does not force performance mode. After removing the accepted date and its surrounding dash separators, conservative venue/location parsing may establish performance metadata only when city plus state/region or country is strongly anchored and no unexplained trailing text remains. For example, Ray Price - Gilley's - Pasadena, Texas - xx-xx-81 becomes Ray Price 1981-xx-xx Gilley's Pasadena, TX. Explicit leading-year Artist - Album commercial-release forms keep their separate rules, and ambiguous album-like text remains an album rather than being forced into performance metadata.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Commercial releases may use (YYYY) - Artist - Album or YYYY - Artist - Album, where YYYY is exactly one four-digit 19xx or 20xx year. TLO uses that year only to recognize the commercial-release form; it does not write the year to DATE or include it in the Show Name. Complete dates, partial dates, year ranges, two-digit years, x-filled years, and years embedded in other text do not qualify. The Show Name is Artist - Album. If the album tail already begins with the same resolved Artist followed by a dash, TLO removes that one redundant Artist component, so Rod Stewart - Rod Stewart - Camouflage becomes Rod Stewart - Camouflage. For tagging, the discovered Album portion is retained as ALBUM_NAME and is used as the base Album tag even when Date, Venue, and Location are blank; it must not fall through to Unknown.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Aggregates related wrapper/part folders such as CD1/CD2/CD3 under one logical show only when every direct music-bearing child under the parent belongs to the same release relationship. If any direct music-bearing sibling is unrelated, TLO keeps the folders separate and never promotes the broad collection/search parent into one show. A short v-number inside a larger descriptive parenthetical, such as (WLIR-FM, rm v.2), is not treated as a volume suffix. The narrow Parent/Parent (1) through Parent (N) multipart-release layout is aggregated only when all direct music-bearing children share the parent-matching base, the part numbers are consecutive from 1, and the parent itself has no direct music. Inventory discovery can continue below a recorded parent music folder so a genuinely independent nested opening act can still become its own show; normal wrapper/grouping rules prevent ordinary discs/sets from being split incorrectly.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Recognizes one additional guarded wrapper layer, such as Show/FLAC/Set 1 and Show/FLAC/Set 2. Set, Disc, Disk, CD, D, Part, Side, and Tape numbered folders may be combined under a non-numbered media container such as FLAC or Audio, and a setlist stored directly in the date-bearing Show folder applies to the complete show. TLO crosses only that validated wrapper layer and checks only files directly in the Show folder. It does not rescan sibling show folders. If unrelated music also exists below the proposed Show folder, TLO does not promote that folder into one show.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- For a date-bearing show, recognizable supplemental/source/media descendants such as Source 2 EXTRAS, Right Channel (Soundboard Feed), Open Mic Lithium, art-docs, Concert Pictures/Video, Disc 1/Flac, and Disc end tracks remain part of the dated show instead of becoming accidental independent shows. TLO keeps the descendant separate when it carries its own complete date or conflicting tagged Artist/AlbumArtist evidence, and it does not absorb a supplemental branch when another unrelated music-bearing branch such as an opening act exists below the dated show. If direct root audio and wrapper/supplemental descendants initially resolve to the same physical show root, they are collapsed into one logical group before tagging or renaming so two workers cannot independently mutate the same folder.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- During a real non-compliant Full Inventory, TLO can consolidate validated non-date sibling collections such as Frankie Valli - Greatest D1/D2 or Pink Floyd - Early Flights/(alt1)/(alt2) into one parent named Frankie Valli - Greatest or Pink Floyd - Early Flights. Dry Run never creates or moves this parent and blocks if an interrupted earlier consolidation requires recovery. A complete performance date excludes the rule. For this sibling-collection decision, xxxx-xx-xx is also treated as a specific date and prevents consolidation, avoiding accidental grouping of distinct unknown-date shows. A year, year span, decade label, or no year is still allowed.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- TLO compares only sibling candidates in the current search on the same partition. D/CD-style suffixes are multipart evidence. alt folders are included only when usable setlist or filename titles show materially different content; identical, overlapping, shifted, or insufficient song lists remain separate alternatives. No other partition is searched for this decision.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- TLO creates a journaled temporary sibling parent, moves only the accepted children into it, concatenates all usable child setlists alphabetically into parent info.txt, and renames the completed parent to the shared release name. A collision or failed operation rolls back safely, and an unresolved interrupted move blocks inventory rather than guessing.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- The new parent and info.txt are inventoried once; the original children remain intact beneath it. Files are ordered one child at a time, including layouts such as D1/FLAC and D2/FLAC, and tagged with one continuous 01-N sequence, or 001-N when there are more than 99 tracks.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Uses selected setlist header metadata for date, artist, venue, and location fallback before track names or hash/checksum sections. Supported strong header shapes include strict unlabeled Artist / Venue, City, State-or-Country / Date; compact Artist Date and Artist Date Venue lines where the date anchors the split; concise Location -- Venue or Venue -- Location; and Artist followed by Live at Venue, City, State/Region/Country, Date. Introductory prose cannot shift the Artist/Venue slots, and a trailing performance date on a Live at line is removed before Venue/Location splitting. Before Artist DB lookup, an explicitly separated terminal performance qualifier is removed from the structured artist candidate, and the same unique-only apostrophe retry used for tag artists is available after an exact miss. An unlabeled or compact artist is accepted only when it resolves uniquely in artists.sqlite. A DB-confirmed structured setlist artist may correct a conflicting artist supported only by weaker generic path/subdirectory scanning, but it does not override $slam, tag-backed artists, explicit commercial/folder patterns, selected-setlist filename artist evidence, or other stronger/non-path artist evidence. A single-word Artist DB hit embedded in a selected-setlist filename is accepted only when the filename has strong positional structure, such as the date being the first substantive component after the artist. Location parsing requires the state/region/country to terminate the location expression, rejects title-like city fragments ending in connectives such as In, At, On, Of, To, or From, accepts safe mixed-case state codes only in strongly delimited forms, and avoids pulling very short venue words out of unrelated longer lines or comma-separated performer lists. A date followed by a double-dash duration remains valid date evidence. Ordinary text sampling is bounded to 1 MiB, full ordinary-text reads above 16 MiB are rejected, and DOCX document.xml content above 16 MiB uncompressed is rejected before decompression.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- Artist DB terminal-suffix fallback is guarded. TLO queries the complete candidate first. Only after a complete-name miss may it strip one terminal Band, Group, All Star/All-Star/All Stars/All-Stars, or the corresponding ... Band form and retry. The shorter name must resolve uniquely and nonterminal occurrences are never stripped. When that fallback succeeds, TLO restores the exact removed suffix for the performance artist unless the DB master already ends in a supported grouping suffix. Restored performance names that are not themselves full Artist DB masters are added to TLOHome/artistsNotInDatabase.txt for review.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Uses eTreeDB and setlist.fm only when enabled, and only to fill blanks or report observations.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Commas in unnumbered song lists do not need to be followed by spaces; TLO treats \u8220\'93Song A,Song B,Song C\u8221\'94 the same as \u8220\'93Song A, Song B, Song C\u8221\'94 when the item count matches the audio files.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8640\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Practical choice: When in doubt, start with non-compliant mode for mixed real-world collections. Use compliant mode when you deliberately organized the folders to match the supported naming patterns and want those names trusted.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
11. Online lookup options}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Online lookup is optional. It is used to fill missing venue/location fields after artist and a full yyyy-mm-dd date are known. Normally, later sources do not overwrite nonblank metadata found earlier. In non-compliant mode, one narrow correction is allowed: higher-confidence selected-setlist venue/location metadata may replace a conflicting value supported only by weaker path-part evidence. eTreeDB and other stronger evidence are not displaced. Other non-equivalent disagreements are reported as observations in the summary log.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- etreeDB checkbox or --etree-lookup: uses eTreeDB first among online sources. When tagging is enabled, the same option can also allow a last-resort eTreeDB song-title lookup if local setlist titles are not usable.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- setlist.fm checkbox or --setlistfm-lookup: in normal matching, uses setlist.fm as a last resort when etreeDB does not return usable venue/location data. On the command line, --setlistfm-lookup requires --etree-lookup. In the GUI, selecting setlist.fm automatically selects etreeDB. When Thorough Setlist Matching is enabled, setlist.fm becomes a proactive evidence source when enabled: TLO may query it even after etreeDB succeeds and may collect additional same-date candidates so they can corroborate or challenge the local/eTree setlist. This broader coverage does not give setlist.fm higher authority.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- setlist.fm requires SETLISTFM_API_KEY in the environment.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Normal setlist.fm access is rate-limited to one request every 600 milliseconds across local workers and capped at 1,400 calls per inventory run. If both setlist.fm and setlist.fm upgrade are checked, TLO instead permits up to 14 requests per second and enforces a shared maximum of 48,000 requests per UTC day across TLO runs using the same TLOHome. Thorough Setlist Matching does not raise these limits by itself: with setlist.fm enabled but upgrade off, better coverage can take substantially longer and may be curtailed by the normal rate/run limits. With upgrade on, Thorough uses the same deconfliction rules but can gather setlist.fm evidence much more aggressively. Upgrade changes coverage/capacity, never setlist.fm authority. Coordination state is stored under TLOHome/logs/setlistfm-state rather than the system temporary directory. If a worker cannot acquire the reservation lock within 20 seconds, TLO records the lookup failure and continues without waiting indefinitely.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- For U.S. lookup results, show names use Artist Date Venue City StateCode. Non-U.S. results use Artist Date Venue City Country.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Thorough Setlist Matching}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Thorough Setlist Matching is a separate accuracy-versus-time choice. It defaults off. With it off, TLO preserves early stopping and the familiar local setlist, eTreeDB, then setlist.fm fallback behavior. With it on, TLO continues gathering reasonable local candidates plus whichever online lookup sources are enabled; etreeDB is included only when etreeDB is checked, and setlist.fm only when setlist.fm is checked. In the main-window Info area, Thorough itself produces no extra message when neither online source is selected; when online sources are selected, the message names only those enabled sources. TLO compares exact-count and near-count (plus or minus two) lists, uses filename and existing Title-tag corroboration, Venue/Location compatibility, and independent-source agreement, and can align recording-only Intro/Tuning/Crowd items or performance-only Encore items without shifting every later track. A strong recording-local list can still beat online consensus when the actual audio supports it; matching eTreeDB and setlist.fm data can beat a weak local parse. If the best two cross-source candidates are nearly tied but materially different, TLO reports an ambiguity rather than silently choosing by precedence.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
When setlist.fm is enabled, Thorough makes setlist.fm proactive even after a usable eTreeDB answer and can inspect additional same-date results. This can take substantially longer under normal setlist.fm access because the ordinary 600-millisecond spacing and 1,400-call run cap still apply. setlist.fm upgrade removes that major coverage/time constraint by allowing the existing upgraded 14-requests-per-second / 48,000-per-UTC-day capacity. Upgrade affects accessibility and coverage only; it never gives setlist.fm greater authority in the final decision.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Command-line equivalent: --thorough-setlist-matching.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
Command-line rule: --compliant and --rename-compliantly cannot be used together; TLO reports an argument error.\line Command-line examples:\line tlo-gi.exe --TLOHome C:\\TLOHome --etree-lookup\line python3 tlo-gi.py --TLOHome "$TLOHome" --compliant --as-is-artist-name --etree-lookup --setlistfm-lookup}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
12. Tagging functions}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The tagging window is used when you want TLO to write tags to audio files. Its title bar uses the installed application version (v1.6 Build 448 in this manual). Inside the window, the single bold heading is Traders Little Helper\u8482\'99 Tagger App; there is no second in-window version heading. The exact layout may vary slightly by platform, but the main choices and actions are the same.}
