\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\qc{\loch\fs18\i\loch
Figure 4. Add Shows window. Dry run and shared settings come from the main Inventory window.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Enter a nonblank Current Backup/Storage Drive and Volume. The TLOCurrentStorage environment variable or --current-storage-volume can prepopulate it.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Add Shows has no separate Preview buttons, no Dry run checkbox, and no duplicated main-option checkboxes. Check for Duplicates remains because it applies only to Process New Shows. Select Dry run on the main Inventory window, then click Process New Shows or Process Potential Duplicate/Upgrades to run the detailed non-destructive analysis. Each action reads the current main-window values when clicked and shows the same complete checkbox-value section in Review Operation before starting.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
After you click Start, TLO appends the reviewed settings to TLOHome/logs/runSettings.log before the action begins. Clicking Go Back or closing Review Operation does not create a log entry. If TLO cannot write the settings log, it reports the problem and does not start the action.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Add Shows does not keep a separate Mode display of copied main-window settings. Review Operation reports every current main-window checkbox in the same labels and order used for Full Inventory and Tag: etreeDB, Compliant, Tag in Place, Artist in Album Tag, setlist.fm, setlist.fm upgrade, Thorough Setlist Matching, Rename Compliantly, Tag Copy, Convert shn, As-Is Artist Name, Tag Copy/Delete Original, and Dry run. If Thorough and setlist.fm are on without upgrade, Review Operation warns that the normal 600-ms / 1,400-call limits can constrain coverage; with upgrade on it notes that upgraded access is available for proactive corroboration/deconfliction. Tag Copy and Tag Copy/Delete Original are reported but marked as not used by Add Shows.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Tag in Place is honored for accepted new and duplicate-resolution folders. Tag Copy and Tag Copy/Delete Original are ignored because Add Shows already has its own readyForXfer, dups, and staged movement workflow.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- If bootlist.csv does not exist, TLO warns that Add Shows is normally used after Full Inventory and asks whether to create the first bootlist from readyForXfer.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- For potential duplicates/upgrades, review the matching existing rows and text files, then choose which old folders to keep or remove. The generated deleteBackupFolders.bat commands use the selected old bootlist paths.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Cross-partition potential-duplicate rule: when Check for Duplicates finds potential matches only on another partition, TLO assumes those old folders are unavailable for comparison and keeps the incoming show as (pdupNN), starting with (pdup01) and advancing beyond the highest existing pdup number for that matching show family. The pdup marker is written into the Show identity, setlist/tag parentheticals, and the folder name when Rename Compliantly is enabled. If any matching row is on the current partition, or TLO cannot determine the partition, the normal potential-duplicate review and existing copy/alternate checks continue unchanged. A pdup marker means potential duplicate only; it does not claim that the recordings are copies or alternates.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
14. Search app}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Launch tlo-gsi from the platform application folder. The Search app uses TLOHome/bootlist.csv for normal searches and TLOHome/setlists for Deep searches.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Use |AND| and |OR| to combine terms; parentheses and quoted phrases are supported.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Normal search treats an empty search box as all bootlist rows. Deep search requires a nonblank term and searches setlist text.}
